{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-u1-equivariant-reduction","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:u1-equivariant-reduction","kind":"proposition","title":"$\\mathrm{U}(1)$-equivariant reduction of the exceptional divisor","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-exceptional-divisor","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-commutative-qou"],"tags":["exceptional-divisor","u1","equivariant","commutative-limit"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.CommutativeQOU.u1EquivariantReduction","text":"u1-equivariant-reduction.md","leanSource":"u1-equivariant-reduction.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:u1-equivariant-reduction\"></a><p>On the exceptional divisor <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{S}_p</code>, restricting observables to those equivariant under the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{U}(1)</code> polar rotation yields the orbit space <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{S}_p / \\mathrm{U}(1) \\cong [0, \\pi]</code>. Over the interior, this simplifies the observable algebra to a free <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{U}(1)</code>-bundle parameterized by a single phase.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/u1-equivariant-reduction.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"4.7.19","page":"b/prop-u1-equivariant-reduction","qa":{"counts":{"pass":87,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":13,"unknown":0,"stale":76},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":1}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Core.u1EquivariantReduction","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/u1-equivariant-reduction.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
